---  
Once `pack` has finished, you can launch the application using `docker run`:
```
$ docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 docker.io/library/myproject:0.0.1-SNAPSHOT
Copied!

```

###  Using GraalVM native-image
Another option to turn an AOT processed Spring Boot executable jar into a native executable is to use the GraalVM `native-image` tool. For this to work, you’ll need a GraalVM distribution on your machine. You can either download it manually on the 
Assuming an AOT processed Spring Boot executable jar built as `myproject-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar` is in the `target` directory, run:
```
$ rm -rf target/native
$ mkdir -p target/native
$ cd target/native
$ jar -xvf ../myproject-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar
$ native-image -H:Name=myproject @META-INF/native-image/argfile -cp .:BOOT-INF/classes:`find BOOT-INF/lib | tr '\n' ':'`
